lfred Sisley",1867,0,0,null,0,"4/4c/Portrait_d%27Alfred_Sisley.jpg/330px-Portrait_d%27Alfred_Sisley.jpg",0,0,1,0,null,"Portrait d'Alfred Sisley",null,"Oil on canvas","28 × 32 cm",50],[137639379,"Young Woman in the Vineyards",1869,0,0,null,0,"f/f1/Jeune_Femme_dans_les_vignes%2C_Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille.jpg/330px-Jeune_Femme_dans_les_vignes%2C_Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille.jpg",0,0,1,0,null,"Jeune Femme dans les vignes | Junge Frau zwischen Weinstöcken | Young Woman among Grapevine","Dep. 0811","Oil on cardboard","27 × 34.9 cm",50],[139759798,"Thérèse reading in the Park at Méric",1867,0,0,null,0,"5/56/TH%C3%89R%C3%88SE_LISANT_DANS_LE_PARC_DE_M%C3%89RIC.PNG/330px-TH%C3%89R%C3%88SE_LISANT_DANS_LE_PARC_DE_M%C3%89RIC.PNG",0,0,1,1,null,null,null,null,null,58],[139762012,"Young Girl at the Piano",1866,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,1,null,null,null,null,null,48],[140995316,"Pot de fleurs",1866,0,0,null,0,"0/0d/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_-_Pot_de_fleurs.jpg/330px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_-_Pot_de_fleurs.jpg",0,0,1,0,null,null,null,"Oil on canvas","100.3 × 80.9 cm",50],[141597171,"Young Woman Playing the Piano",1867,0,0,null,0,"5/5a/Bazille_-_Jeune_fille_au_piano._186667%2C_Lot_3203.jpg/330px-Bazille_-_Jeune_fille_au_piano._186667%2C_Lot_3203.jpg",0,0,1,0,null,null,null,"Oil on canvas",null,50]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":3,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"325981":["The Family Reunion or Portraits of the Family is an oil-on-canvas painting executed in 1867 by the French painter Frédéric Bazille. It is the largest surviving canvas by this artist.","The Family Reunion (painting)"],"2786992":["View of the Village is an oil-on-canvas painting created in 1868 by the French Impressionist Jean-Frédéric Bazille, now in the Musée Fabre in Montpellier.","View of the Village"],"2868852":["Atelier de la rue Furstenberg is an 1866 oil-on-canvas painting by the 19th century French impressionist artist Frédéric Bazille, which has been in the collection of the Musée Fabre in Montpellier, France since 1985.","Studio on Rue Furstenberg"],"3212360":["The Pink Dress is an oil-on-canvas painting by Frédéric Bazille, produced in 1864 when he was aged 23. The work is now in the Musée d'Orsay, in Paris.","The Pink Dress"],"4442468":["La Toilette is an oil-on-canvas painting by the 19th century French impressionist artist Frédéric Bazille, executed in 1869–1870, which has been in the collection of the Musée Fabre in Montpellier, France since 1968. He produced it a few months before his death in the Franco-Prussian War in 1870.","La Toilette (Bazille)"],"7439713":["Scène d'été, Summer Scene, or The Bathers is an oil-on-canvas painting by the French artist Frédéric Bazille from 1869. It is now in the Fogg Art Museum in Cambridge, Massachusetts.","Scène d'été"],"12142552":["Portrait of Pierre‑Auguste Renoir is an oil on canvas portrait painted in 1867 by the French artist Frédéric Bazille (1841–1870). The work depicts the young French painter Pierre‑Auguste Renoir (1841–1919), who later became a key figure in the Impressionist movement.","Portrait of Pierre‑Auguste Renoir"],"15876329":["The Improvised Field Hospital or Monet after His Accident at the Inn of Chailly is an oil-on-canvas painting created in 1865 by the French painter Frédéric Bazille.","The Improvised Field Hospital"],"15877622":["Bazille's Studio is an oil-on-canvas painting created in 1870 by the French Impressionist Frédéric Bazille. The painting is also known as L'Atelier de la rue Condamine, The Studio, and The Studio on the Rue La Condamine.","Bazille's Studio"],"15879724":["Black Woman with Peonies also known as Négresse aux pivoines, Young Woman with Peonies, or Negress with Peonies, is a pair of paintings created by the French Impressionist painter Frédéric Bazille in the spring of 1870.","Black Woman with Peonies"],"20188677":["Portrait of Édouard Blau is an oil-on-canvas painting executed in 1866 by the French painter Frédéric Bazille. The work depicts the French writer and librettist Édouard Blau.","Portrait of Édouard Blau"],"20891094":["Landscape by the Lez River is an oil-on-canvas landscape painting by the 19th-century French impressionist artist Frédéric Bazille, completed in 1870. It is the collection of the Minneapolis Institute of Arts.","Landscape by the Lez River"],"104881668":["Femme en costume Mauresque is an oil-on-canvas painting by the 19th-century French impressionist artist Frédéric Bazille, completed in 1869. It has been in the collection of the Norton Simon Museum in Pasadena, California, since 1997.","Femme en costume Mauresque"],"115652311":["Ruth et Booz is an oil-on-canvas painting by the 19th-century French impressionist artist Frédéric Bazille, executed in 1870, which has been in the collection of the Musée Fabre in Montpellier, France since 2004.","Ruth et Booz"],"139759798":["Thérèse reading in the Park at Méric is an oil on canvas painting executed in 1867 by the French artist Frédéric Bazille (1841–1870). The work depicts a young woman, identified as Bazille’s cousin Thérèse des Hours, seated outdoors in the grounds of the Méric estate, absorbed in reading a book.","Thérèse reading in the Park at Méric"],"139762012":["Young Girl at the Piano by Frédéric Bazille (1841–1870) is in a private collection and not part of a public museum's permanent holdings. The painting, an oil on canvas executed around 1866–1867, measures approximately 40.5 × 32.5 cm and is signed by the artist.","Young Girl at the Piano"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}